(Gender Classification) Tj
0 -11 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(Tangkhul distinguishes biological and social gender through suffixed markers.) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(Linguistic Rules & Examples:) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(  * Human Masculine: -mayar / -va \(e.g., ngalava -> youth/man, naomayar -> boy/son\).) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(  * Human Feminine: -shanao / -la \(e.g., shanaonao -> girl/daughter, ava -> mother\).) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(  * Animal Gender: Male suffix -khon / -mayara \(simuk-mayara [bull]\), Female suffix -lui / -shanao \(simuk-lui [cow]\).) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 7 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -9 Td
/F2 9 Tf
