(Tense and Aspect Suffixes) Tj
0 -11 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(Tangkhul verbs carry inflectional suffixes indicating tense, aspect, and completion.) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(Linguistic Rules & Examples:) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(  * Root verbs take prefix ka- / kha- in citation/infinitive form: kasa \(to do\), kazat \(to go\), kapam \(to sit\).) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(  * Present Simple / Habitual: -i / -ya \(e.g., I zat-ya -> I go\).) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(  * Present Continuous: -da lei \(e.g., I pam-da lei -> I am sitting / waiting\).) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(  * Past Perfective: -ser-re / -haowa \(e.g., Ana zat-haowa -> He has departed\).) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(  * Future Tense: -ra \(e.g., Ithum shok-ra -> We will come out / emerge\).) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(  * Imperative: -lu \(positive: Salu -> Do it!\), -kha \(negative: Masalu -> Don't do it!\).) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 7 Tf
