(Negative Particles) Tj
0 -11 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(Negation in Tangkhul is achieved primarily through the circumfix ma-...-mana.) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(Linguistic Rules & Examples:) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(  * Declarative Negation: ma- [verb root] -mana \(e.g., I ma-thei-mana -> I do not see/know\).) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(  * Stative Negation: ma-kalei \(is not / does not exist\) vs lei \(exists\).) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(  * Prohibitive Imperative: ma- [verb root] -alu \(e.g., Ma-zat-alu -> Do not go!\).) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 7 Tf
( ) Tj
0 -9 Td
/F2 9 Tf
(Interrogative Particles) Tj
0 -11 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(Questions end with interrogative enclitics.) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(Linguistic Rules & Examples:) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(  * Polar \(Yes/No\) questions: -la? \(e.g., Na pamra-la? -> Will you stay?\).) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(  * Wh-Questions: Khi \(what\), Kachida \(where\), Khipa \(who\), Khitharan \(when\), Khipakha \(why\).) Tj
0 -10 Td
