(Basic Constituent Order \(SOV\)) Tj
0 -11 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(Tangkhul strictly adheres to Subject-Object-Verb \(SOV\) typology with head-final syntactic trees.) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(Linguistic Rules & Examples:) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(  * Standard word order: Subject + Object + Verb \(e.g., Mayarnao-na [S] kharai [O] phungda lei [V] -> The man is carrying the basket\).) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(  * Modifier precedes or follows based on category: Demonstratives precede, numerals and adjectives follow head nouns.) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 8 Tf
(  * Honorific and polite particles: -sho, -rei, -meo signify mutual respect between kin and elders.) Tj
0 -10 Td
/F1 7 Tf
